{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4cZ2KfJQ5ActvUED5oe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LRKsouXeot8WxXeBp4CSCJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":100,"limit":50},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2733,"cache_read_input_tokens":177827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2733},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e2c1f70-53aa-4703-b5b7-cf3bec7d6ad2","uuid":"49d84730-6e19-40b6-8ca6-1d6af49422d6","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:12:25.248Z","request_id":"req_011Ch4cZ25Xhm1tmjcvqW6Rd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LRKsouXeot8WxXeBp4CSCJ":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":100,"limit":50}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LRKsouXeot8WxXeBp4CSCJ","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t- An explicit disable writes at most one `learning_rail_disabled` event per\n101\t  session and switch.\n102\t\n103\t### Changed — `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md`: two closed enums gain values\n104\t\n105\t- `learning_rail_disabled.rail` gains `bash_indirect`, and `.switch` gains\n106\t  the two switch names above. No event and no field is added. A consumer\n107\t  that pins the old enum lists rejects the new values.\n108\t- The row's prose still calls ADR-201 `PROPOSED`; the ADR is `ACCEPTED`.\n109\t\n110\t### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n111\t\n112\t- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n113\t  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n114\t  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n115\t  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,\n116\t  `audit-query.py`, `check_contamination.py` and\n117\t  `check-installer-write-safety.py` move the same way.\n118\t- Installs and upgrades receive the packages: the installer copies every\n119\t  `_lib` entry except the test harness. On the merge of pull request #7,\n120\t  the Smoke Install push run passed; a manually dispatched run was\n121\t  cancelled.\n122\t- If you patched a hook by hand, the entry point no longer holds the logic.\n123\t  Re-apply the patch to the module.\n124\t- The compatibility evidence is the test suites. No differential replay\n125\t  against the code before the split is claimed.\n126\t\n127\t### Changed — a registered hook leaves its spool work pending at exit (ADR-055-AMEND-4, partial)\n128\t\n129\t- `_python-hook.sh` exports `CEO_HOOK_BOUNDED_EXIT=1`. A hook that runs\n130\t  with it does not drain its audit spool at exit or on a signal. It leaves\n131\t  an `exit_deadline_skip` breadcrumb instead, and its events wait in the\n132\t  spool for a later drain, so they can reach the log later.\n133\t- This removes the forced exit drain that could outlast a hook's timeout.\n134\t- ADR-055-AMEND-4 is `ACCEPTED` with its implementation `PARTIAL`\n135\t  (Known-open).\n136\t\n137\t### Security and governance — what changed without the signing ceremony\n138\t\n139\t- **How it arrived.** Pull requests #6 and #7 brought 233 canonical paths\n140\t  into `main` with no sentinel and no signature file. Fifteen of them are\n141\t  kernel paths by the kernel list as merged: among them the Bash-guard,\n142\t  canonical-edit, pair-rail, policy and audit-writer hooks, the\n143\t  agent-frontmatter VETO validator, the Codex pin file, the framework's own\n144\t  settings and `validate.yml`. By the list this release restores (Fixed,\n145\t  below), 101 of them are. The merge commit of #7 carries a GPG signature,\n146\t  which is not the signing ceremony. No signed sentinel ratifies those\n147\t  files as of this entry, and nothing in the repository requires one:\n148\t  `main` has no branch protection and no ruleset (measured through the\n149\t  GitHub API on 2026-11-03)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e2c1f70-53aa-4703-b5b7-cf3bec7d6ad2","uuid":"d803d6a9-f162-4de6-a610-5afb8436b575","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:12:25.275Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"- An explicit disable writes at most one `learning_rail_disabled` event per\n  session and switch.\n\n### Changed — `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md`: two closed enums gain values\n\n- `learning_rail_disabled.rail` gains `bash_indirect`, and `.switch` gains\n  the two switch names above. No event and no field is added. A consumer\n  that pins the old enum lists rejects the new values.\n- The row's prose still calls ADR-201 `PROPOSED`; the ADR is `ACCEPTED`.\n\n### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n\n- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,\n  `audit-query.py`, `check_contamination.py` and\n  `check-installer-write-safety.py` move the same way.\n- Installs and upgrades receive the packages: the installer copies every\n  `_lib` entry except the test harness. On the merge of pull request #7,\n  the Smoke Install push run passed; a manually dispatched run was\n  cancelled.\n- If you patched a hook by hand, the entry point no longer holds the logic.\n  Re-apply the patch to the module.\n- The compatibility evidence is the test suites. No differential replay\n  against the code before the split is claimed.\n\n### Changed — a registered hook leaves its spool work pending at exit (ADR-055-AMEND-4, partial)\n\n- `_python-hook.sh` exports `CEO_HOOK_BOUNDED_EXIT=1`. A hook that runs\n  with it does not drain its audit spool at exit or on a signal. It leaves\n  an `exit_deadline_skip` breadcrumb instead, and its events wait in the\n  spool for a later drain, so they can reach the log later.\n- This removes the forced exit drain that could outlast a hook's timeout.\n- ADR-055-AMEND-4 is `ACCEPTED` with its implementation `PARTIAL`\n  (Known-open).\n\n### Security and governance — what changed without the signing ceremony\n\n- **How it arrived.** Pull requests #6 and #7 brought 233 canonical paths\n  into `main` with no sentinel and no signature file. Fifteen of them are\n  kernel paths by the kernel list as merged: among them the Bash-guard,\n  canonical-edit, pair-rail, policy and audit-writer hooks, the\n  agent-frontmatter VETO validator, the Codex pin file, the framework's own\n  settings and `validate.yml`. By the list this release restores (Fixed,\n  below), 101 of them are. The merge commit of #7 carries a GPG signature,\n  which is not the signing ceremony. No signed sentinel ratifies those\n  files as of this entry, and nothing in the repository requires one:\n  `main` has no branch protection and no ruleset (measured through the\n  GitHub API on 2026-11-03).","numLines":50,"startLine":100,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LRKsouXeot8WxXeBp4CSCJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4cZ2KfJQ5ActvUED5oe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R3XokCcvE1wxeo8fDPGs9U","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":645,"limit":40},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2733,"cache_read_input_tokens":177827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2733},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e2c1f70-53aa-4703-b5b7-cf3bec7d6ad2","uuid":"cbacda7e-764a-4ffb-beb3-0444b4bd0753","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:12:27.342Z","request_id":"req_011Ch4cZ25Xhm1tmjcvqW6Rd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01R3XokCcvE1wxeo8fDPGs9U":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":645,"limit":40}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R3XokCcvE1wxeo8fDPGs9U","type":"tool_result","content":"645\t  id; run the command it prints to see the list.\n646\t- The `codex_invoke.py` example and the default label of\n647\t  `optimizer/codex_phase_gate.py` move to `gpt-5.6-sol`.\n648\t\n649\t### Fixed — `audit-query.py`, `/status`, `/ceo-boot` and `check-substrate-drift.py`\n650\t\n651\t- `audit-query.py`: the shared flags (`--log`, `--include-rotated`,\n652\t  `--json`, `--csv`, `--errors-path`) now take effect before or after the\n653\t  subcommand. Before, the subcommand's default silently replaced a value\n654\t  given BEFORE the subcommand. For example, `audit-query.py --log X summary`\n655\t  summarized the default (live) log as if it were X, and `--json summary`\n656\t  printed a table.\n657\t- `/status` reported health as `UNKNOWN` on every run. `status.py` called\n658\t  `audit-query.py health` with a flag that does not exist (`--as-json`); it\n659\t  now passes `--json`.\n660\t- `/ceo-boot`:\n661\t  - A plan in `executing` with no commit in 24 hours is listed as waiting,\n662\t    not stranded, when it declares its wait (`external_wait`, or a\n663\t    `## Blockers` section with content).\n664\t  - The false red of `scheduled_workflows_red` is cured as a class. The\n665\t    check makes one request per scheduled workflow under one 4-second\n666\t    budget, and stale or undated data is yellow, never red.\n667\t- `/ceo-boot --verbose` adds an advisory Tier-A check,\n668\t  `tier_a_model_currency`, that is never red. Installs do not receive\n669\t  ADR-149, so in an install this check always answers green with\n670\t  `sem dado` (no data). Its summary text is in Portuguese.\n671\t- `check-substrate-drift.py`: a substrate ledger that is valid JSON of the\n672\t  wrong shape (`components` not a list, `last_seen` not an object) used to\n673\t  replace the whole report with `DETECTOR_ERROR`, hiding a Codex drift\n674\t  already found. Each component (Codex, Claude Code, the catalog) is now\n675\t  checked on its own. A ledger of the wrong shape is a named\n676\t  `CC_LEDGER_UNREADABLE` (unknown), a component whose check raises is a\n677\t  named `COMPONENT_CHECK_ERROR` (unknown), and in both cases `--strict`\n678\t  still exits 1 on the other components' drift. This cures a P2 finding of\n679\t  the v1.4.2 GA re-pass. `/ceo-boot` does not run this tool.\n680\t\n681\t### Added — read-only audit verifiers\n682\t\n683\t- `.claude/scripts/audit_spool_state.py` inspects the audit spool's state\n684\t  directory."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e2c1f70-53aa-4703-b5b7-cf3bec7d6ad2","uuid":"a82be8a9-268e-4e10-88e5-281af2ea070c","timestamp":"2026-11-15T11:12:27.369Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.tG8bbW/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  id; run the command it prints to see the list.\n- The `codex_invoke.py` example and the default label of\n  `optimizer/codex_phase_gate.py` move to `gpt-5.6-sol`.\n\n### Fixed — `audit-query.py`, `/status`, `/ceo-boot` and `check-substrate-drift.py`\n\n- `audit-query.py`: the shared flags (`--log`, `--include-rotated`,\n  `--json`, `--csv`, `--errors-path`) now take effect before or after the\n  subcommand. Before, the subcommand's default silently replaced a value\n  given BEFORE the subcommand. For example, `audit-query.py --log X summary`\n  summarized the default (live) log as if it were X, and `--json summary`\n  printed a table.\n- `/status` reported health as `UNKNOWN` on every run. `status.py` called\n  `audit-query.py health` with a flag that does not exist (`--as-json`); it\n  now passes `--json`.\n- `/ceo-boot`:\n  - A plan in `executing` with no commit in 24 hours is listed as waiting,\n    not stranded, when it declares its wait (`external_wait`, or a\n    `## Blockers` section with content).\n  - The false red of `scheduled_workflows_red` is cured as a class. The\n    check makes one request per scheduled workflow under one 4-second\n    budget, and stale or undated data is yellow, never red.\n- `/ceo-boot --verbose` adds an advisory Tier-A check,\n  `tier_a_model_currency`, that is never red. Installs do not receive\n  ADR-149, so in an install this check always answers green with\n  `sem dado` (no data). Its summary text is in Portuguese.\n- `check-substrate-drift.py`: a substrate ledger that is valid JSON of the\n  wrong shape (`components` not a list, `last_seen` not an object) used to\n  replace the whole report with `DETECTOR_ERROR`, hiding a Codex drift\n  already found. Each component (Codex, Claude Code, the catalog) is now\n  checked on its own. A ledger of the wrong shape is a named\n  `CC_LEDGER_UNREADABLE` (unknown), a component whose check raises is a\n  named `COMPONENT_CHECK_ERROR` (unknown), and in both cases `--strict`\n  still exits 1 on the other components' drift. This cures a P2 finding of\n  the v1.4.2 GA re-pass. `/ceo-boot` does not run this tool.\n\n### Added — read-only audit verifiers\n\n- `.claude/scripts/audit_spool_state.py` inspects the audit spool's state\n  directory.","numLines":40,"startLine":645,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R3XokCcvE1wxeo8fDPGs9U","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
