rs: a hand fix in the facade copy changes nothing at runtime. This is the trap condition 7 warns about, inside the facade itself.\\n- Honesty: the docstring at :123, \\\"Lesson validation remains delegated to `_validate_boot_lesson`\\\", has nothing to do with this function. It exists only so that test_dead_symbol_lesson_render_safe_is_gone (`\\\"_validate_boot_lesson\\\" in src`) still passes.\\n- Minimal fix: delete the facade copy and the docstring sentence. Have the test take the function from `_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/model_persona.py`, or from `dict(mod.TIER_A_CHECKS)` of the loaded facade.\\n\\nP2-3 — .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py:180-184 and .claude/scripts/check-vacuous-checks.py:133 (checks that read the text of ceo-boot.py now see almost nothing)\\n- The vacuous-check lint scans .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py by default. It now sees 2 check_* functions instead of every boot check, including the new main_checkout_state. test_cli_clean_on_real_ceo_boot therefore passes trivially, and its docstring's promise (a new vacuous check turns it red) no longer holds.\\n- Two text-presence tests now pass on marker comments, whether or not the registry still wires the check:\\n  - test_plan_091_expected_callsites.py:133-146, through `# Tier-S 16th entry: check_tier_policy_misrouting_24h (\\\"tier_policy_misrouting_24h\\\")`;\\n  - test_ceo_boot_audit_emit.py:93-95, through `# === PLAN-065 Phase 2 audit_emit wire ===`.\\n  The facade comment says openly that the markers are there for these checks.\\n- Minimal fix: make the lint's default input the facade plus `_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/*.py`. Make the tests load the module and assert registry membership, for example `\\\"tier_policy_misrouting_24h\\\" in dict(mod.TIER_S_CHECKS)`. Then drop the markers.\\n\\nP2-4 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:174-250 (check_hook_live_smoke, moved unchanged)\\n- Failure: the check runs py_compile only on the registered entry points. After PLAN-197 those are short facades that compile `_lib/*_parts/*.py` at import; check_bash_safety.py:35-42 is an example.\\n- Scenario: an adopter re-applies a hand patch to a part file, as the CHANGELOG asks, and introduces a syntax error, or a part file is missing. The hook crashes at import, `_python-hook.sh` lets the tool call through (an infrastructure fault fails open), and hook_live_smoke still reports green \\\"N hook(s) smoke-pass\\\". Before the split, the same broken logic sat in the hook file and showed red as `compile_fail`.\\n- This widens a blind spot that already existed: the check never compiled the `_lib` modules that hooks import.\\n- Minimal fix: also run py_compile on every file in each facade's `_PARTS` tuple (read by AST), or on every .py under the `_lib` subpackages, and report a missing part as `missing:`.\\n\\nP2-5 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:25-26\\n- Each part starts with a docstring. When it runs in the facade's dictionary, it overwrites __doc__, so ceo_boot.__doc__ becomes \\\"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\\\". This is cosmetic; argparse uses an explicit description.\\n- Minimal fix: save and restore __doc__ around install(), or remove the part docstrings.\\n\\nP2-6 — stale pointers\\n- .claude/hooks/SessionEnd.py:662 (`ceo-boot.py::_validate_boot_lesson`) and docs/threat-model.md:2423 still point at ceo-boot.py. The function now lives at .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/candidates_lessons.py:405.\\n- The facade's module docstring (\\\"15 Tier-S checks\\\", \\\"per-check timeout 500 ms\\\") was already stale in the base and is now 25 checks out of date.\\n- Minimal fix: update the references.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\\nNone. No undeclared P1 was found in this payload.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\\nP2-1 through P2-6 above. P2-1 and P2-4 come from moved text whose assumptions PLAN-197 changed: same text, different behavior. P2-2 and P2-3 reduce what this release's test suites prove about ceo-boot, and the CHANGELOG names those suites 